Focused Cpp Gate3 run 28139776079 on pushed e23003d4 moved past the optional Array<Int>/Null<Int> first blocker in TestBasetypes.testArray. The new first ordered Cpp compile errors start in generated TestMain.cpp:12767 inside TestBasetypes.testString.

Current generated surface includes:

  eq(String::fromCharCode(77), "M");
  eq((std::string() + std::string("x")), "nullx");
  eq((std::string("x") + std::string()), "xnull");
  auto abc = "abc".split("");
  eq((abc[0]), "a");
  eq(static_cast<int>(static_cast<unsigned char>(str[(-1)])), nullptr);
  eq(sentence.substr(5, 2), "my");

The first failures are std::string vs const char[] equality, string literal method lowering for split, Haxe String null-concat semantics currently rendered as empty std::string, and Haxe string indexing/null/out-of-range behavior. Contain the string basetype surface narrowly enough to move the first ordered Cpp Gate3 blocker. Preserve earlier progress: TemplateWrap diagnostics remain moved, Kilometer::fromMeter m.get() remains fixed, MyHash<V>::MyHash keeps __hxhx_make_shared_StringMap<V>(), MyVector helper returns stay std::shared_ptr<MyPoint3>, MyAbstractSetter no longer emits (*this) = __hxhx_anon{}, and TestBasetypes.testArray optional vector helpers remain in place.

Focused Cpp Gate3 run 28138262925 on pushed b09a4e9e moved past MyAbstractSetter anonymous self assignment. The new first ordered Cpp compile errors start in generated TestMain.cpp:12700 inside TestBasetypes.testArray:

  eq((a.size()), 3);
  eq((a[0]), 1);
  eq((a[3]), nullptr);
  a.remove(2);
  a_2.splice(1, 1);

The current generated type is std::vector<std::optional<int>>, which exposes several C++ mismatches at once: size_t vs Int equality, std::optional<int> vs Int/null equality, out-of-bounds/null Haxe Array access semantics, and Haxe Array remove/splice methods emitted as native std::vector methods.

Contain this optional-array/basetype surface narrowly enough to move the first ordered Cpp Gate3 blocker. Preserve earlier Cpp Gate3 progress: TemplateWrap diagnostics remain moved, Kilometer::fromMeter m.get() remains fixed, MyHash<V>::MyHash keeps __hxhx_make_shared_StringMap<V>(), MyVector helper returns stay std::shared_ptr<MyPoint3>, and MyAbstractSetter no longer emits (*this) = __hxhx_anon{}.

Later failures remain out of scope unless naturally reached: broader string basetype helpers, class-constant/typeof raw StringMap factories, raw IntMap/Map factories, abstract construction/operator lowering for MyVector usages, and primitive abstract method calls on erased ints.

